Below is a step-by-step set of SQL statements that start with locating Abakan’s airport, look at the flights that use it, add the corresponding coordinates and finally calculate the great-circle distance for every such route so that we can pick the longest one.  
(The point column keeps the coordinates as (longitude , latitude).  
The radius of the earth is taken as 6 371 km.)

```sql
--Description: 1) Find the Abakan airport code(s).
SELECT DISTINCT airport_code,
       city ->> 'en' AS city_en,
       coordinates
FROM airports_data
WHERE city ->> 'en' LIKE '%Abakan%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show flights that DEPART from Abakan.
SELECT DISTINCT flight_no,
       departure_airport,
       arrival_airport
FROM flights
WHERE departure_airport IN (
      SELECT airport_code
      FROM airports_data
      WHERE city ->> 'en' LIKE '%Abakan%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Show flights that ARRIVE to Abakan.
SELECT DISTINCT flight_no,
       departure_airport,
       arrival_airport
FROM flights
WHERE arrival_airport IN (
      SELECT airport_code
      FROM airports_data
      WHERE city ->> 'en' LIKE '%Abakan%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Add both airports’ coordinates for every flight that involves Abakan.
SELECT DISTINCT f.flight_id,
       dep.airport_code AS dep_code, dep.coordinates AS dep_coord,
       arr.airport_code AS arr_code, arr.coordinates AS arr_coord
FROM flights AS f
JOIN airports_data AS dep ON dep.airport_code = f.departure_airport
JOIN airports_data AS arr ON arr.airport_code = f.arrival_airport
WHERE dep.city ->> 'en' = 'Abakan'
   OR arr.city ->> 'en' = 'Abakan'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Compute the great-circle distance (km) for each individual flight.
SELECT DISTINCT f.flight_id,
       6371 * acos(
           cos(radians(dep.coordinates[1])) *
           cos(radians(arr.coordinates[1])) *
           cos(radians(arr.coordinates[0]) - radians(dep.coordinates[0])) +
           sin(radians(dep.coordinates[1])) *
           sin(radians(arr.coordinates[1]))
       ) AS distance_km
FROM flights AS f
JOIN airports_data dep ON dep.airport_code = f.departure_airport
JOIN airports_data arr ON arr.airport_code = f.arrival_airport
WHERE dep.city ->> 'en' = 'Abakan'
   OR arr.city ->> 'en' = 'Abakan'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Aggregate by route (origin-destination pair) and order by distance.
SELECT DISTINCT dep.airport_code AS from_code,
       arr.airport_code AS to_code,
       MAX(
           6371 * acos(
               cos(radians(dep.coordinates[1])) *
               cos(radians(arr.coordinates[1])) *
               cos(radians(arr.coordinates[0]) - radians(dep.coordinates[0])) +
               sin(radians(dep.coordinates[1])) *
               sin(radians(arr.coordinates[1]))
           )
       ) AS distance_km
FROM flights AS f
JOIN airports_data dep ON dep.airport_code = f.departure_airport
JOIN airports_data arr ON arr.airport_code = f.arrival_airport
WHERE dep.city ->> 'en' = 'Abakan'
   OR arr.city ->> 'en' = 'Abakan'
GROUP BY dep.airport_code, arr.airport_code
ORDER BY distance_km DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Return the single longest distance (km) of any Abakan-involving route.
SELECT MAX(
         6371 * acos(
             cos(radians(dep.coordinates[1])) *
             cos(radians(arr.coordinates[1])) *
             cos(radians(arr.coordinates[0]) - radians(dep.coordinates[0])) +
             sin(radians(dep.coordinates[1])) *
             sin(radians(arr.coordinates[1]))
         )
       ) AS longest_distance_km
FROM flights AS f
JOIN airports_data dep ON dep.airport_code = f.departure_airport
JOIN airports_data arr ON arr.airport_code = f.arrival_airport
WHERE dep.city ->> 'en' = 'Abakan'
   OR arr.city ->> 'en' = 'Abakan';
```

